  "coverage": [
    {"reason":"States the investor-protection purpose; creates no separate approval condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u0.2"},
    {"reason":"Sets UCITS post-authorisation scope and home-supervision context; immediate effect is qualified by the express commencement provision.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u1.190"},
    {"reason":"Identifies the subject of the measures.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u2.523"},
    {"reason":"Confirms that the listed measures concern post-authorisation matters.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},
    {"reason":"Separate relief for changes of depository and investment delegates does not replace the conditions governing material investment changes.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u4.653"},
    {"reason":"Removes prior approval conditionally on home compliance, subject to novelty, complexity and potential local-policy exceptions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},
    {"reason":"Aligns notification periods and content with home requirements; does not abolish notifications.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u6.1221"},
    {"reason":"Identifies implementing FAQs, forms and checklists whose substantive contents are absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u7.1419"},
    {"reason":"Introduces implementation provisions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u8.1677"},
    {"reason":"Specifies commencement on 2025-11-28.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},
    {"reason":"Preserves the existing process for applications received before commencement with approval or authorisation outstanding.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},
    {"reason":"Identifies management companies as the actors addressed by continuing oversight; the heading alone does not specify additional duties.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u11.2030"},
    {"reason":"Preserves SFC post-vetting of changes and filed revised documents, including changes without prior approval, and discretionary enquiries or regulatory action for non-compliance.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"},
    {"reason":"Provides relevant SFC case officers as a clarification channel.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u13.2377"},
    {"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u14.2489"},
    {"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u15.2518"},
    {"reason":"Defines covered funds by domicile and UCITS status, including UK UCITS.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},
    {"reason":"FAQ reference supplies no substantive implementing rules in this packet.","status":"UNCERTAIN","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u18.2831"},
    {"reason":"Forms and checklists reference supplies no substantive requirements in this packet.","status":"UNCERTAIN","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"}
  ],
  "dimensions": [
    {
      "dimension":"scope",
      "explanation":"The reading concerns post-authorisation material changes to an investment objective, policy or restriction of a covered UCITS fund. These are alternative categories of change; all three need not change simultaneously. Initial authorisation and operator changes are separate matters.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u4.653","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"definitions",
      "explanation":"Covered funds are UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, and UK-domiciled collective investment schemes authorised as UK UCITS. Materiality, novelty, complexity and potential local policy implications remain undefined. Local policy is interpreted as Hong Kong policy. Applying these terms requires judgment and potentially implementing guidance.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],
      "status":"AMBIGUOUS"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"exceptions",
      "explanation":"Home-jurisdiction compliance is a positive condition of relief. Novel product features, complex product features or possible local policy implications each independently exclude relief; actual policy harm need not be established. Pre-commencement pending applications remain under the existing process even where the substantive change would otherwise qualify.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"modality",
      "explanation":"The measure conditionally removes the SFC's prior-approval requirement. Exceptions preserve the otherwise applicable requirement rather than create a blanket prohibition. Home compliance does not necessarily mean home-regulator approval; the source does not prescribe that equivalence. Notification requirements remain relevant. The SFC will continue post-vetting and may make enquiries or take appropriate regulatory action for non-compliance.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u6.1221","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"time",
      "explanation":"The express effective date, 2025-11-28, governs the introductory reference to immediate effect. The transition is interpreted as testing outstanding approval or authorisation at commencement, although the assessment time is not expressly stated. SFC receipt before that date, rather than submission alone, is specified. Receipt on that date is not receipt before it. Withdrawal, refiling and modification of pending applications remain unaddressed.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"dependencies",
      "explanation":"Earlier uncertainty remains concerning applicable home requirements, the existing approval process, implementing FAQs, forms and checklists, and case-specific fund, change and application facts. Dependencies missing.1c25ffdf5c1e10e0297748d5 and missing.79fb54125bb1f35a1d457fad have no supplied contents. Neither their rules nor the linked materials' contents are inferred.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u7.1419","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u18.2831","d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"],
      "status":"AMBIGUOUS"
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What are the fund's domicile, UCITS status and SFC authorisation status, and what material change is proposed?",
    "Does the change meet applicable home requirements, involve novel or complex product features, or potentially have Hong Kong policy implications?",
    "When is the change to occur, and did the SFC receive a relevant application before 2025-11-28 with approval or authorisation outstanding at commencement?",
    "What do the existing approval process and relevant FAQs, forms and checklists require for this case?"
  ],
  "readings": [
    {
      "assumptions": [
        "The express commencement and transition provisions qualify the introductory statement of immediate effect.",
        "Outstanding approval or authorisation is assessed at commencement for the transition; that assessment time is not explicit.",
        "Investment objectives, policies and restrictions denote alternative categories of material change.",
        "Local policy implications refers to Hong Kong policy implications.",
        "Exclusion from relief leaves the otherwise applicable prior-approval requirement intact; the circular does not supply every underlying approval rule.",
        "The previous reading has been checked against all supplied units, including all three footnotes. No case-specific facts or external implementing contents have been supplied."
      ],
      "citations": [
        {
          "quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"
        },
        {
          "quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"
        },
        {
          "quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"
        },
        {
          "quote":"For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"
        },
        {
          "quote":"To align the SFC’s notification requirements with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, including the notice periods and content requirements.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u6.1221"
        },
        {
          "quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"
        }
      ],
      "distinction":"The actual question answered is when this circular removes prior SFC approval for a material investment change and when it preserves the existing requirement or application process. This is a conditional textual interpretation, not a Boolean compliance, prohibition, licence-possession or eligibility result. Formalization remains null because a complete case-specific approval determination depends on missing underlying rules and the preserved application process; a relief predicate alone would answer a narrower question. Missing facts remain unknown.",
      "family":"exceptions",
      "formalization":null,
      "local_id":"reading.ucits_prior_approval",
      "questions":[
        "How do the implementing FAQs distinguish novel or complex features and potential local policy implications?",
        "What approval does the existing process require for the particular excluded or transitional change, and how does it treat withdrawal, refiling or modification?"
      ],
      "statement":"From 2025-11-28, this circular removes prior SFC approval for a covered UCITS fund's post-authorisation material change to an investment objective, policy or restriction if the change complies with home-jurisdiction requirements, involves neither novel nor complex product features, and has no potential local policy implications, subject to the application transition. Covered funds are UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, and UK-domiciled collective investment schemes authorised as UK UCITS. Novelty, complexity or possible Hong Kong policy implications each excludes relief; failure to satisfy home requirements likewise leaves the otherwise applicable approval requirement in place. Home compliance must be established under the applicable home rules, not assumed from home supervision alone. If the SFC received an application before 2025-11-28 and approval or authorisation remained outstanding at commencement, the SFC continues processing it under the existing process even if the change would otherwise qualify for relief. This does not itself establish the outcome of that process or automatically dispose of the application. Management companies remain subject to applicable notification and filing requirements, whose full content is not supplied. The SFC continues post-vetting and may make follow-up enquiries or take regulatory action for non-compliance. The particular approval outcome for an excluded or transitional case remains dependent on the existing rules and missing implementing materials.",
      "subject":"Conditional removal or preservation of prior SFC approval for material UCITS investment changes"
    }
  ]
}
